From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Wed, 1 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: make the generic reset_cpu() weak

The K230 resets through a register in its system controller. Make the
generic reset_cpu(), used when SYSRESET is disabled, weak so that SoC
code can provide its own.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 arch/riscv/cpu/cpu.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/cpu/cpu.c b/arch/riscv/cpu/cpu.c
index 15c4e145..e5e03ac5 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/cpu/cpu.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/cpu/cpu.c
@@ -724,7 +724,8 @@ __weak void harts_early_init(void)
 }
 
 #if !CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(SYSRESET)
-void reset_cpu(void)
+/* __weak so SoC code (e.g. arch/riscv/cpu/k230/cpu.c) can provide its own. */
+__weak void reset_cpu(void)
 {
 	printf("resetting ...\n");
 
-- 
2.43.0

